@startuml CAP_Security_Model
!theme plain

title CAP Protocol - Security and Trust Model

actor "Agent (LLM)" as agent
participant "Host\n(Session + Timeline)" as host
participant "Plugin Server\n(Separate Process)" as server
database "Filesystem" as fs

== Trust Levels ==

note over agent : **Untrusted**\nDSL calls go through\nhost permission system
note over host : **Trusted**\nOwns graph, controls\nprocess spawning
note over server : **Semi-trusted**\nSeparate process,\ncapability-gated access

== Permission Boundaries ==

agent -> host : DSL: v = shell("pytest")
activate host
host -> host : Check shell\npermission
host -> server : node/create("shell", ["pytest"])
activate server
server --> host : NodeCreateResult
deactivate server
host --> agent : Node created
deactivate host

== Filesystem Access via Roots ==

server -> host : host/query_roots()
activate host
host --> server : roots: [{uri: "file:///project", name: "cwd"}]
deactivate host

server -> host : host/resolve_root("file:///project", "src/main.py")
activate host
host -> host : Validate root URI\nCheck path traversal
host -> fs : Resolve real path
fs --> host : /project/src/main.py
host --> server : { real_path, exists: true }
deactivate host

== Capability Gating ==

server -[#red]x host : <color:red>host/create_node (BLOCKED)\nif create_node: false</color>
note over host : PERMISSION_DENIED (-32004)

== Sandboxing ==

note over server
  **Process Isolation**
  - Separate OS process
  - Minimal privileges
  - Resource limits (CPU, memory, I/O)
  - No network unless declared
  - No secrets via initialize
  - Input validation on both sides
end note

@enduml
